From: (local patch, not an upstream commit) QM1 Debian Maintainers <qm1-debian@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 00:15:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] rtl8723bs: reinit the TX completions to keep
 complete()/wait counts balanced

The xmit thread waits for SdioXmitStart, which is completed every time a
frame is enqueued.  Since v5.9 complete() is a counting semaphore, i.e.
complete() increments the counter of the completion and the waiter
decrements it.  The driver never re-arms the completion, so that count
is never reset and a residue makes the wait return immediately instead
of sleeping, which makes the xmit thread busy-loop.  The same applies to
xmit_comp, which is re-armed by the previous patch in this series.

Re-arm SdioXmitStart after the wait.  The pending state is checked right
after the wait, so a kick that is consumed by the re-arm does not lose
any frame.
---
 drivers/staging/rtl8723bs/hal/rtl8723bs_xmit.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/rtl8723bs/hal/rtl8723bs_xmit.c b/drivers/staging/rtl8723bs/hal/rtl8723bs_xmit.c
index cc53c91..f8a56a5 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/rtl8723bs/hal/rtl8723bs_xmit.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/rtl8723bs/hal/rtl8723bs_xmit.c
@@ -413,6 +413,13 @@ static s32 rtl8723bs_xmit_handler(struct adapter *padapter)
 		return _FAIL;
 	}
 
+	/*  Re-arm the completion.  Since v5.9 complete() is a counting
+	 *  semaphore: complete() increments the counter, the waiter
+	 *  decrements it.  The driver never re-arms it, so a residue
+	 *  makes the wait above return immediately and the xmit thread
+	 *  busy-loops instead of sleeping. */
+	reinit_completion(&pxmitpriv->SdioXmitStart);
+
 next:
 	if (
 		(padapter->bDriverStopped) ||
